{"text": "March 17, 1988\n\nMr. d. F. Anders\nMr. J. E. Menn, dr.\n\nR. D. Chumney, dr,\n\nProject NXM (MONTCLAIR)\n\nReferring to my memo to you dated February 18 on the above subject, I requested\ndevelopment of a king size MXM model with increased tobacco strength for further\nconsumer testing. Recent lab work has indicated that MXH-4A blend produced a\nstronger smoke taste with more impact than the previously tested MXM-2A blend.\n\nMarketing appears at the present to be more interested in a 100-nm product. There~\nfore, please prepare a 100-nm model delivering 16+ to 17-mg \u201ctar\u201d using KXM-6A blend\nfor consumer testing versus Doral Full Flavored 100's cigarettes. The 100-mn MXM\nmodel should be constructed similar to AMERICAN 100's - China and PALL MALL Red\nFilter Cigarettes.\n\nTesting 1s to be conducted in a blind paired-comparison format among approximately\n50 Kinston, 50 Marlboro and 20 Doral 100's full-flavored smokers. We will require\n50 cartons each of our model and Doral 100's, both averwrapped and packaged in white\nASTP wrapping materials.\n\nWe will not require king size MXM models for consumer testing at this time.\n\nmt\n\ncc? ORB, DEC, UGB, ROC", "words": [{"text": "March", "x0": 56, "y0": 93, "x1": 90, "y1": 103, "conf": 86.0}, {"text": "17,", "x0": 100, "y0": 93, "x1": 118, "y1": 105, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "1988", "x0": 128, "y0": 93, "x1": 155, "y1": 103, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "Mr.", "x0": 56, "y0": 121, "x1": 75, "y1": 132, "conf": 84.0}, {"text": "d.", "x0": 85, "y0": 121, "x1": 97, "y1": 132, "conf": 75.0}, {"text": "F.", "x0": 106, "y0": 121, "x1": 118, "y1": 132, "conf": 64.0}, {"text": "Anders", "x0": 127, "y0": 121, "x1": 168, "y1": 132, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "Mr.", "x0": 56, "y0": 136, "x1": 75, "y1": 146, "conf": 78.0}, {"text": "J.", "x0": 84, "y0": 136, "x1": 97, "y1": 146, "conf": 78.0}, {"text": "E.", "x0": 106, "y0": 136, "x1": 118, "y1": 146, "conf": 56.0}, {"text": "Menn,", "x0": 127, "y0": 136, "x1": 160, "y1